          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Small-group project:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Pick at least one of the following. Make groups of 8 to 10. Collect data individually as needed. Put together everyone’s data and do the appropriate analysis and visualisation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.613,
            0.847,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Our heights vs. our family’s heights: Collect the heights of your family members."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.656,
            0.846,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Make a dot plot showing heights of just your family members. Describe its variability and central tendency."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.229,
            0.7,
            0.846,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Make a double-bar graph showing each student’s height next to their family’s mean height."
